To efficiently find the unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2 using MATLAB, you can follow these steps:

1. Read the text files into MATLAB.
2. Convert the text to lowercase and split it into words.
3. Find the unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2.
4. Print the unique words.

Here's an implementation in MATLAB that can handle a large amount of text:

```matlab
function unique_words = find_unique_words(text1_file, text2_file)
    % Read the text files into MATLAB
    text1 = fileread(text1_file);
    text2 = fileread(text2_file);

    % Convert text to lowercase and split into words
    words1 = lower(strsplit(text1));
    words2 = lower(strsplit(text2));

    % Find unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2
    unique_words = setdiff(words1, words2);
end
```

You can call this function with the file names as arguments:

